Algorithm

Step 1: Start the program.
Step 2: Initialize an empty stack and an empty queue.
Step 3: Display the menu with the following options:
Add a bus stop.
Remove the last added bus stop.
Search for a bus stop.
Display all bus stops.
Exit.
Step 4: Read the user's choice.
Step 5: Perform the selected operation.
Add Stop: Insert the new stop into the stack and queue.
Remove Stop: Remove the most recently added stop from the stack and update the queue.
Search Stop: Search for the specified stop in the route.
Display Stops: Display all stops in their original route order.
Exit: Terminate the program.
Step 6: If the user enters an invalid choice, display an error message.
Step 7: Repeat Steps 3–6 until the user chooses Exit.
Step 8: Stop the program.
